he steeplechase, placing fifth of 15 teams in the riding. The Soviets won the riding, but Hungary won the fencing easily to move into a big lead. Hungary also won the shooting phase, which pretty much settled the gold medal. The USSR won the swimming and placed second in cross-country running but could not catch the Hungarians. The two teams were so dominant, however, that France, in third place, trailed the Soviet Union by almost 1,000 points."] "\n\n" [:p {} "However, it was actually closer than that. Sweden originally finished third, only 60 points behind the Soviet Union. But one of their athletes, " [:a {:href "/athletes/35071"} "Hans-Gunnar Liljenvall"] ", failed a doping test for alcohol, and became the first Olympic athlete to be disqualified for the use of drugs. Liljenvall declared that he had only had two beers. Olympic historian Volker Kluge has noted that his blood alcohol level was 0.4."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Team Points"] [:th {} "Individual Points"] [:th {} "Adjusted Individual Points"] [:th {} "Riding"] [:th {} "Fencing"] [:th {} "Shooting"] [:th {} "Swimming"] [:th {} "Running"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Hungary"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HUN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HUN.png"}] "HUN"]] [:td {} "14,325"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2,940 (5)"] [:td {} "3,130 (1)"] [:td {} "2,714 (1)"] [:td {} "2,877 (6)"] [:td {} "2,664 (4)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34843"} "András Balczó"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "14,325"] [:td {} "4,953"] [:td {} "5,022"] [:td {} "2,940"] [:td {} "3,130"] [:td {} "2,714"] [:td {} "2,877"] [:td {} "2,664"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""